    "durationMs": 211116,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Stack**: ASP.NET Core 8.0 minimal API (`net8.0`, C# 12) with EF Core 8.0.15 + Npgsql 8.0.11 — the idiomatic .NET persistence layer for the provided PostgreSQL 16.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `POST /links` — validates url (absolute http/https with host) and optional code (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`), returns `201 {\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}` echoing the URL unchanged, generates a unique 8-char code when omitted, `409` on duplicate custom code, `422` on malformed JSON/missing url/invalid url/invalid code.\n- `GET /links/{code}` — `200` with link or `404 {\"error\":...}` for unknown codes (pattern-invalid codes return `422`).\n- `GET /r/{code}` — `302` with `Location` set to the stored URL; clicks incremented atomically via `ExecuteUpdateAsync` (exactly once per hit).\n- `GET /links` — `{\"items\":[...],\"total\":n}` in ascending creation order.\n- `DATABASE_URL` (PostgreSQL URL form) is parsed at runtime into an Npgsql connection string — credentials are never hard-coded; query params like `sslmode` pass through.\n\n**Verified by live HTTP tests**: all creation/validation/404/409/422 cases, redirect Location header, click counts incrementing 0→1→3, and full persistence across a server restart (fresh process loaded identical data and click counts).\n\n**Delivery**: `sh start.sh` builds (incremental), applies pending migrations via `dotnet ef database update` (with `Database.Migrate()` at startup as a safety net), then execs the server in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`. README documents startup and the API. I left the database freshly migrated and empty, and no stray server processes running, so the graded run starts clean."
